# Postgres (RDS) — local / agent usage

## Connection

Credentials live in **repo-root `.env`** (gitignored). Standard libpq variables:

- `PGHOST`, `PGPORT`, `PGUSER`, `PGPASSWORD`, `PGDATABASE`

RDS requires TLS from many networks. Prefer:

```bash
export PGSSLMODE=require
```

## Run `psql` with env loaded

From repo root:

```bash
set -a && source .env && set +a
export PGSSLMODE=require
./scripts/psql-with-env.sh
```

Or one-shot SQL:

```bash
set -a && source .env && set +a
export PGSSLMODE=require
./scripts/psql-with-env.sh -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -f path/to/script.sql
```

`scripts/psql-with-env.sh` loads `.env` and invokes Homebrew `psql` if needed.

## Migrations and seeds in-repo

- **`lambdas/shared/run-migration.js`** — creates tables, runs `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` for additive changes, seeds idempotently. Needs AWS Secrets Manager access to Postgres credentials (same as deployed Lambdas), unless you override with env.
- **`lambdas/shared/patch-add-initial-page-id-to-built-in-applets.sql`** — idempotent column add for `built_in_applets.initial_page_id`.
- **`lambdas/shared/seed-built-in-applets.sql`** — reference seed for `sigma_org_config` and `built_in_applets`.

## Schema note: built-in landing page

`built_in_applets.initial_page_id` (nullable) is the Sigma **page id** for first paint when opening a built-in applet from the app list (tap-to-open). The generate-url Lambda still receives `page_id` in the **request body**; the mobile app passes it from navigation params sourced from this column when set.

## AWS

RDS access may require VPN or corporate network. If the agent cannot reach the host, run the same SQL locally or use the AWS console query editor. For Lambda deploys and CLI patterns, see **`aws-cli-usage.mdc`**.
